        {
          "segment_index": 0,
          "entry_id": "possessive-ui",
          "context_en": "의 connects Gildong to his father: ‘Gildong’s father’. 길동 is the reviewed shortened name of 홍길동."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 2,
          "entry_id": "topic-eun-neun",
          "context_en": "는 sets Gildong’s father as the topic: the sentence tells us what work he did."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 4,
          "entry_id": "possessive-ui",
          "context_en": "의 connects the country to its important work, referring here to work for the country."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 6,
          "entry_id": "modifier-eun",
          "context_en": "중요한 describes the following noun 일: ‘important work’. This is a descriptive modifier, not a completed action."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 8,
          "entry_id": "object-eul-reul",
          "context_en": "을 marks 일 as the work that his father did."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 10,
          "entry_id": "past-ass-eoss",
          "context_en": "하다 becomes 했다 in the past; 하였 contracts to 했. His father did this work before the time of narration."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 10,
          "entry_id": "polite-seumnida",
          "context_en": "했습니다 presents the past action ‘did’ in the narrator’s formal polite style."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 12,
          "entry_id": "topic-eun-neun",
          "context_en": "는 makes Gildong's mother the topic: the sentence explains her role in the household."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 16,
          "entry_id": "action-location-eseo",
          "context_en": "에서 marks the household as the place where his mother worked."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 18,
          "entry_id": "present-action-modifier-neun",
          "context_en": "일하는 modifies 사람: a person who works. The modifier describes her work at the time of the past-tense statement, so the natural English translation is 'who worked.'"
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 20,
          "entry_id": "copula-ida",
          "context_en": "이다 connects his mother with 사람이, identifying her as a person who worked in that household; 이 here belongs to the copula, not a subject particle."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 20,
          "entry_id": "past-ass-eoss",
          "context_en": "었 places her role as a household worker in the past."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 20,
          "entry_id": "polite-seumnida",
          "context_en": "습니다 ends the statement about his mother's former role in a formal, polite style."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 24,
          "entry_id": "topic-eun-neun",
          "context_en": "는 sets his mother as the topic: the sentence explains her relationship to his father."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 26,
          "entry_id": "possessive-ui",
          "context_en": "의 connects 아버지 to 아내: ‘his father's wife.’"
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 28,
          "entry_id": "negative-complement-i-ga",
          "context_en": "가 marks 아내 as the role denied by 아니다: his mother was not his father's wife."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 30,
          "entry_id": "past-ass-eoss",
          "context_en": "The past form 아니었다 places the statement about her status in the past."
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 30,
          "entry_id": "polite-seumnida",
          "context_en": "-습니다 ends 아니었습니다 as a formal polite statement; the meaning remains ‘was not.’"
        },
        {
          "segment_index": 34,
          "entry_id": "topic-eun-neun",
